.TH DEVTOOL 1 "2026-07-01" "devtool 0.2.16" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
devtool \- generic Unix developer helper CLI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B devtool
.RI [ global-options ] command " [command-options]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
devtool applies artifacts, validates repositories, summarizes restore/build/test output,
copies logs to the clipboard, sends notifications, writes Tasker JSON events, and automates
common repository tasks.
.PP
Global options are placement-tolerant where possible, so options such as
.BR --yes ,
.BR --repo ,
.BR --copy ,
and
.B --machine-file
may be placed before or after the subcommand.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B restore | build | test | validate | wine-validate | run | package
Run project actions from .devtool.toml or detected project defaults.
.TP
.B test --no-build
Run tests while passing
.B --no-build
to
.B dotnet test
when the resolved test command is a dotnet test command.
.TP
.B validate
Run restore, build, and test. When validation has already built the target, implicit dotnet test commands use
.B --no-build
so the test phase does not rebuild the same target.
.TP
.B apply-overlay | apply-snapshot
Apply an artifact to a repository. Options include
.BR --validate ,
.BR --validate-only ,
.BR --preview ,
.BR --diff ,
.BR --interactive ,
.BR --commit ,
.BR --skip-restore ,
.BR --skip-build ,
and
.BR --skip-test .
.TP
.B batch
Run a sequence of steps such as validate or apply-overlay=/path/to/file.zip.
.TP
.B config show | defaults | resolve | doctor
Inspect configuration.
.TP
.B status | doctor
Show repo and tool status. Use
.B doctor --fix
to create safe state/cache/XDG data directories.
.TP
.B detect | handoff | history | rollback | targets
Inspect repository shape, generate handoff notes, show artifact history, revert a recorded commit, or list configured targets.
.TP
.B logs latest
Show or print the latest saved raw log.
.TP
.B completion zsh
Print zsh completion.
.TP
.B init-config
Write a .devtool.toml template into a repository root.
.TP
.B tag | release-notes | commit
Git helper commands.
.TP
.B ai-prompt
Generate a fully resolved AI workflow prompt for the current repository.
.SH TRANSACTIONAL ARTIFACT APPLY
Before mutating files for
.B apply-overlay
or
.BR apply-snapshot ,
devtool creates an rsync backup of only the paths the artifact will touch. For overlays this includes changed archive members and paths listed in
.BR .devtool-delete .
Unchanged archive members and devtool metadata files are not backed up.
.PP
If extraction, delete handling, restore, build, test, or an interruption fails after the transaction begins, devtool rolls the touched paths back from the backup. Rollback is a normal devtool result: stdout summaries, notifications, clipboard output, Tasker progress/events, and machine JSON are still emitted.
.PP
If the process is force-closed and leaves an active transaction marker, the next devtool command for that repository detects the stale transaction, rolls it back, emits normal output/JSON/notifications, and exits non-zero so the original command can be rerun.
.PP
Successful applies and successful rollbacks remove the transaction backup directory. The original overlay/snapshot artifact and sidecar manifest are deleted only after the complete apply/validate/commit flow succeeds without rollback. If rollback happens, the artifact is preserved for debugging or retry.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -y , " --yes"
Assume yes for confirmations, including dirty repository and artifact prompts.
.TP
.BR --force
Force dangerous actions such as non-git repository operation.
.TP
.BR --machine "[=compact|pretty]"
Emit the machine JSON envelope on stdout.
.TP
.BR --machine-file " FILE"
Write the machine JSON envelope to FILE without changing normal stdout.
.TP
.BR --copy , " --copy-summary" , " --copy-json"
Copy raw output, rendered summary, or JSON summary.
.TP
.BR --tasker , " --tasker-progress" , " --tasker-dir" , " --tasker-broadcast"
Write Tasker-compatible state/event JSON under the configured Tasker directory and optionally broadcast Android intents.
.TP
.BR --notify-progress
Update a live Termux notification while command phases run.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/devtool/logs
Saved raw command logs.
.TP
.I ${XDG_DATA_HOME:-~/.local/share}/devtool
XDG devtool data directory. Transaction state and rsync backups are stored under
.I transactions/<repo-key>/
while active. Set
.B DEVTOOL_XDG_DIR
to override this location.
.TP
.I .devtool.toml
Per-repository configuration.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DEVTOOL_XDG_DIR
Override the XDG devtool data directory for transaction state and backups.
.TP
.B DEVTOOL_PROJECT_*
Overrides [project] values from .devtool.toml.
.TP
.B DEVTOOL_ENV_*
Overrides or injects runtime env vars from [env].
.SH AUTHOR
OpenAI
